A||||5||griff||Front end question||||5||
Z||000000||griff||12-24-2001||05:59 PM||||I have a 88 Fiero coupe with 80k miles. There is a rattling noise in the front end.  I replaced the front shocks and that did not solve the problem. The rattling occurs while driving on rough roads or hitting a bump.  Any ideas on where to start first? ||||reg||5
Z||000001||mrfiero||12-24-2001||06:21 PM||||It could be bad bushings or bad balljoints.<P>It could also be that the upper control arm shaft has loosened up a bit (not unconmmon).  This is usually due to the deterioration of the bushings.<P>Jack up the car and remove the front wheels.  On the upper shaft are some big washers (at each end).  If these washers can be spun by hand then the nuts have backed off a bit.  Re-tighten the nuts and that should solve (at least temporarily) your rattling problem.<P>You might also want to check out the balljoints.  Put the wheels back on (or do this before taking them off) and grab the wheel at the 3 & 9 o'clock positions.  Wiggle back and forth while a helper is under the front end watching the balljoints......any movement at the spindle (where the balljont attaxches) is bad.  Replace the balljoints.<P>Note:  if one lower balljoint is bad, replace them both.  I always replace balljoints in pairs. <P>The upper balljoints don't wear as fast, so I doubt they are bad.  The lowers, even if they aren't bad yet, are probably in need of replacing at 80K miles.<P>LMK what you find out.  I have owned about a dozen '88 Fieros since 1990 and have rebuilt/worked on the suspensions many times.||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||12-24-2001||08:57 PM||||Id also look for something really obvious around the front, jack or spare loose, radiator brackets broke, headlite mechanism, sway bar loose............etc. try to move everything you see, titen up anything loose.||||reg||1
Z||000003||tesmith66||12-25-2001||09:26 AM||||Could also be sway bar end links or loose pads in the brake calipers.<P>------------------<BR>Timothy E. Smith<BR>1986 SE V6<BR>1984 Coupe||||reg||1
Z||000004||Rodney||12-25-2001||10:56 AM||||I had a nasty irritating rattle on the passenger side on my 88 Mera. When I had it up on jack stands one day I went around and hit stuff with my hand. It was the passenger side cooling tube. I made a clamp and also put some rubber between the tube and the body. Rattle gone. What a relief!||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||12-25-2001||01:16 PM||||It could be anyhing listed above and more.<P>The inner brake pad has a clip attached to it that may have broken. Unusual but posible.<P>Sway bar is a good call... those things commonly puke out a bushing. Can drive you nuts when that happens. also affects handling...<P>make sure the jack spare etc in the front is tight. The jack handle isn't locked down in anyway... it could bounce and make noise. Trap it to the jack with a big rubber band to eliminate that posibility.<P>look around up front and make sure someone didn't drop any thing that's now bouncing around loose.||||reg||1
